==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|aɪvə(r)|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{label|en|slang}} A [[banknote]] with a value of five units of currency.
#: ''Do you have a '''fiver''' I could borrow? I can pay you back tomorrow.''
# By extension: the value in money that this represents.
#: ''I bought the chocolates; they were only a '''fiver'''.''
# A clenched fist.
# A mathematical puzzle played on a 5 &times; 5 grid.
# {{label|en|Islam}} A [[Zaydi]] Shiite Muslim, who disagrees with the majority of Shiites on the identity of the Fifth Imam.
# {{label|en|religion}} A person who gives five percent of their income or five hours a week of their time to charity (a reduction of ten percent [[tithing]]).

